# MASTER BUILD PROMPT — EXCEL FORMULA FORENSICS & BACKTRACKING ENGINE

## 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Build a production-quality Python application called:

**Excel Formula Forensics & Backtracking Engine**

The purpose of the application is to take an Excel workbook, allow the user to select any formula cell, and visually explain **exactly how Excel arrives at the final value**.

The application must behave like a combination of:

1. Excel Formula Evaluator
2. Formula Debugger
3. Dependency Tree Explorer
4. Data Lineage Engine
5. Formula Audit Engine
6. Financial Model Review Tool
7. Formula Anomaly Detector
8. Impact Analysis Tool
9. Interactive Calculation Flowchart

The core principle is:

> **Every number must have an explainable lineage.**

The application must not merely show that Cell F2 depends on Cell A2. It must explain:

* What the original formula is
* Which functions are inside the formula
* Which arguments each function receives
* Where those arguments come from
* Which rows/cells were matched
* Which branches of IF/IFS were executed
* Which branches were not executed
* What intermediate values were produced
* How arithmetic was performed
* Which source cells contributed to the final result
* Whether errors or anomalies exist
* Whether the formula is consistent with surrounding formulas
* What would be affected if an input cell changes

